# Legacy /previous-artists deep links — gh (static) target only.
#
# The old site served per-artist pages at /previous-artists/{slug}, and later
# at /previous-artists/single/{slug}. Both shapes survive in the wild (Discogs,
# forums, old press), so both must reach today's
# /records/artists/previous/single/{slug}.
#
# On the cf target these are handled in src/middleware.ts
# (legacyPreviousArtistTarget) instead, NOT here and NOT via
# astro.config.mjs's `redirects`. Reason: the Cloudflare adapter writes config
# redirects into this file in static-hosting shape —
# @astrojs/underscore-redirects appends "/index.html" to every dynamic
# destination — and that suffix 404s on an SSR Worker (verified on staging:
# clean path 200, /index.html form 404). The static-asset layer answers before
# the Worker, so those generated rules hijacked exactly the URLs they were
# meant to rescue. Declaring corrected copies alongside them is rejected
# outright: "Invalid _redirects configuration: Duplicate rule for path".
#
# GH Pages ignores this file entirely (no server-side redirects there; Astro
# emits <meta http-equiv="refresh"> pages for its own `redirects` entries), so
# these two lines are documentation-of-intent for that target rather than
# something it executes. They are kept because this file IS honoured on
# Workers Static Assets — DEPLOY.md still claims otherwise, which is stale and
# is being corrected separately.
#
# Keep in sync with legacyPreviousArtistTarget() in src/lib/cache-policy.ts.
/previous-artists/single/:slug  /records/artists/previous/single/:slug  301
/previous-artists/:slug         /records/artists/previous/single/:slug  301
